---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LanguageSwitch from '../../components/LanguageSwitch.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Coaching Examples | Thomas Kolonko"
  description="Two illustrative examples show how business coaching and operational mentoring can support people facing challenges at work."
  language="en"
  alternatePath="/Moegliche-Coaching-Beispiele/"
>
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-50 bg-stone-50/90 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-stone-200/80">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 h-20 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/en/" class="font-serif text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-slate-900">
        Thomas Kolonko <span class="text-stone-400 font-sans text-sm font-normal ml-1 hidden sm:inline">| Coaching & Mentoring</span>
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
        <LanguageSwitch language="en" deHref="/Moegliche-Coaching-Beispiele/" enHref="/en/coaching-examples/" />
        <a href="/en/" class="hidden sm:inline text-sm font-medium text-slate-600 hover:text-emerald-800 transition-colors">
          Home
        </a>
        <a href="/en/#kontakt" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-3 sm:px-5 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium text-white bg-emerald-800 hover:bg-emerald-900 rounded-lg transition-colors shadow-xs">
          <span class="sm:hidden">Call</span><span class="hidden sm:inline">Introductory call</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="py-20 md:py-28 px-6">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mb-14">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800 mb-3">A look at coaching</p>
          <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-slate-900 leading-tight tracking-tight mb-6">
            Two examples of possible coaching topics
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Coaching is as individual as the people and situations clients bring. The following examples are
            fictional and intended as a guide. They illustrate possible conversations – not fixed processes
            or guaranteed outcomes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <article class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-stone-200/90 shadow-xs">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800 mb-3">Collaboration & leadership</p>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-slate-900 mb-6">
              Preparing for a difficult conversation as a project lead
            </h2>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">The situation</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                  A project lead finds that team agreements are repeatedly not being kept. She wants to address
                  this without putting further strain on the collaboration, and she has no formal authority
                  over the team.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Possible coaching work</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                  First, we sort through what is happening and what matters to her. Together, we explore
                  different perspectives, clarify her scope for action and prepare a conversation that is
                  both clear and respectful.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-stone-200 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              <strong class="text-slate-900 font-medium">A possible next step:</strong>
              With a clear concern and a suitable opening, she can approach the conversation herself and
              reflect afterwards on what changed as a result.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-stone-200/90 shadow-xs">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800 mb-3">Resilience & self-regulation</p>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-slate-900 mb-6">
              Finding direction amid constantly changing demands
            </h2>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">The situation</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                  A specialist faces frequent changes in priorities and finds himself thinking about work at
                  home. He wants to handle the pressure better and discover where he can make a difference.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Possible coaching work</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                  Together, we distinguish what is within his influence and what is not. He can explore which
                  thoughts and reactions increase the pressure. Beliefs such as “I have to get everything done”
                  or “Saying no will disappoint others” may come up. We can examine how helpful these thoughts
                  are and what more balanced perspectives might open up. He can also notice his own warning
                  signs and explore personal resources and helpful boundaries.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-stone-200 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              <strong class="text-slate-900 font-medium">A possible next step:</strong>
              A small, self-chosen experiment – such as actively clarifying a priority or consciously wrapping
              up at the end of the working day – can create new experiences.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-900 text-white">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Your situation is unique</h2>
          <p class="text-emerald-50 leading-relaxed mb-6">
            In a free introductory call, we can talk without obligation about what is on your mind and whether
            working together feels right for both of us.
          </p>
          <a href="/en/#kontakt" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-950 bg-white hover:bg-stone-100 rounded-lg transition-colors">
            Arrange a free introductory call
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="bg-stone-100 border-t border-stone-200/80 py-8 px-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <a href="/en/" class="font-serif text-slate-800 font-medium hover:text-emerald-800">Thomas Kolonko</a>
        · Business, resilience & life coaching · Zurich
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-6">
        <a href="/en/legal-notice/" class="hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Legal notice</a>
        <a href="/en/privacy/" class="hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Privacy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
